Interconnect®Interconnect utilization across PCIe, C2C, and NVLink. If any link is near its throughput ceiling, that interconnect is a bottleneck â€” check if transfers can be overlapped with compute (using streams), reduced in volume, or eliminated via persistent device-side data.
If throughput is unexpectedly high during compute-only phases, data may be allocated in system memory and accessed directly rather than residing in device DRAM."ý
