Instruction Cache Hit Rates‡GCC instruction cache hit rate. If low, the combined instruction footprint across warps exceeds GCC capacity â€” reduce kernel code size by limiting unrolling, inlining, or splitting large kernels. Very low rates (<90%) can add visible stall cycles to every warp."}
