L2 Hit Miss per Source UnitÇPer-source-unit hit and miss sector counts at L2. Pair with L2 Bandwidth per Source Unit to see both the total traffic volume and its cache effectiveness in absolute terms.
If L1TEX misses dominate, SM data accesses are not being served by L2 â€” reduce the working set or improve temporal reuse.
If GCC or HUB misses are significant, constant/instruction or system traffic is polluting L2 â€” unusual for compute and worth investigating memory placement.␀"‚
