L1 Data Cache & LSU␀"Ï
L1TEX LSU Throughput½Compare the LSUs two stages to classify the bottleneck.
If LSU Data-Stage > LSU Writeback, the bottleneck is in address processing â€” likely poor coalescing (global/local/surface) or bank conflicts (shared). Check per-space breakdown below and Shared Memory Bank Conflicts.
If LSU Writeback > LSU Data-Stage, wide uniform loads (64/128-bit) or high miss traffic is saturating the writeback path â€” check L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Hit Miss."|
Lpmsampling:l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedLSU Data-StageJgb20x_TriageCompute_sampling"w
Hpmsampling:l1tex__lsu_writeback_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedLSU WritebackJgb20x_TriageCompute_sampling"—	
%L1TEX LSU Throughput per Memory Space¡Identify which memory space drives high LSU throughput.
High LGDS wavefronts indicate heavy local/global/DMA/surface traffic â€” break this down further in SM Memory Bandwidth per Space.
High Shared Misc indicates shuffles, redux, match, or S2R operations saturating the pipe.
High Surface wavefronts may indicate surface load/store overhead â€” consider switching to global loads where image filtering is not needed."†
