Bandwidth per Memory SpaceïCompare absolute bandwidth across memory spaces. The tallest bar is generating the most L1 traffic.
High Local Memory traffic usually indicates register spilling â€” check SM Register Occupancy and consider reducing register usage.
High Global Memory traffic is expected for memory-bound workloads â€” check coalescing efficiency in Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Operation.
High Texture traffic is typical for read-only data with spatial locality â€” verify texture hit rates in L1TEX Sector Hit Rate."c
