L1TEX Data OccupancyâShows how the 128KB per-SM on-chip SRAM is divided between shared memory and L1 data cache. If Shared Memory dominates and occupancy is low, the per-CTA shared-memory allocation is the binding occupancy limiter â€” check Per-CTA Resource Usage. If Tagged Cache is small, L1 hit rates may suffer â€” see L1 Data Cache & LSU for cache-efficiency diagnosis.␀"
