Shared Memory Bank Conflicts€Direct measurement of bank-conflict throughput per operation. A high %-of-peak here means a large fraction of shared-memory pipeline cycles are consumed replaying conflicting accesses.
Bank conflicts occur when multiple threads in a warp access the same 4-byte bank (address % 128 / 4). Common fix: pad shared arrays by one element per row, or transpose the indexing pattern so consecutive threads hit consecutive banks.
Check Shared Bank Conflict Ratios for the average conflicts-per-request for each operation."™
