Constant Cache Hit Rates¢Hit rates for the constant cache hierarchy. Low rates indicate cache pressure from too many unique constant addresses.
Low DCC Hit Rate: reduce the number of distinct constant buffer regions, or pack frequently-used constants together.
Low IDC Hit Rate: indexed constant lookups are scattered â€” consider using constant memory only for truly uniform data, and read-only global memory (__ldg) for per-thread lookups.
Low GCC Constant Hit Rate: constant miss traffic is reaching L2 â€” this significantly increases latency for constant-heavy code."ã
*TriageCompute.sm__average_dcc_hit_rate.pctDCC Hit RateJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzˆTriageCompute.sm__average_dcc_hit_rate = RatioMetric(sm__dcc_requests_lookup_hit, RollupOp.avg, sm__dcc_requests, RollupOp.avg, 1.0, '')"R
