GCC BandwidthýOverview of the GCC (Global Constant Cache), the mid-level cache serving constant data, instructions, and texture/surface descriptors.
If GCC Miss Bandwidth is large relative to GCC Bandwidth, the working set of constants or instructions exceeds GCC capacity â€” drill into the per-type rows below.
If L2 Sectors from GCC is significant, GCC misses are contributing to L2 pressure â€” this is unusual for typical compute workloads and may indicate very large shader binaries or many unique constant addresses.␀"Û
-TriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes.sum.per_secondGCC BandwidthJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzüTriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes = CounterMetric(128 * gcc__cache_requests_type_instruction + 64 * gcc__cache_requests_type_constant + 32 * gcc__cache_requests_type_tsheader, '# of bytes GCC cached') TriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes:SetSustainedRate(128.0)"´
9TriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes_lookup_miss.sum.per_secondGCC Miss BandwidthJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÄTriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes_lookup_miss = CounterMetric(128 * gcc__cache_requests_type_instruction_lookup_miss + 64 * gcc__cache_requests_type_constant_lookup_miss + 32 * gcc__cache_requests_type_tsheader_lookup_miss, '# of bytes GCC cached that missed') TriageCompute.gcc__cache_bytes_lookup_miss:SetSustainedRate(128.0)"r
=pmsampling:lts__t_sectors_srcunit_gcc_realtime.sum.per_secondL2 Sectors from GCCJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingÙn
L2 Cache␀"´
L2 Bandwidth per Source UnitÁIdentify which unit is driving L2 traffic. The dominant bar is the primary L2 consumer.
L1TEX dominates (typical): SM load/store/texture misses are the primary L2 consumer â€” optimize L1 hit rates in the L1 Data Cache & LSU group.
GCC is significant: constant or instruction cache pressure is spilling to L2 â€” check Constant & Instruction Caches group.
CE is significant: host-device DMA transfers are contending for L2 bandwidth â€” check if transfers can be overlapped or reduced.
HUB is significant: system-level traffic (e.g. page table walks) is consuming L2 bandwidth.␀"t
