Blocks Active›The live count of CTAs occupying SM block slots. If Average Blocks Active is low relative to the hardware maximum (24 per SM), the workload is too small or blocks are too resource-heavy. Compare with SM Register Occupancy and Per-CTA Resource Usage to identify the limiting resource."q
:pmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage Blocks ActiveJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"o
:pmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Blocks ActiveJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"º
CGAs Launched & CompletedÆTrack Cooperative Grid Array launches and completions. CGAs coordinate multiple blocks that co-reside on the same GPC. If CGA launches are zero, the workload does not use this feature. If non-zero, compare launches with completions â€” a persistent gap hints at CGA scheduling overhead or resource contention at the GPC level."h
