SM Occupancy & Stalls␀"’
SM Register OccupancyÙCheck whether registers are the occupancy limiter. If Register Occupancy is near 100% while Warps Inactive (SM Active) is high, too many registers per thread prevent additional warps from being resident. Avg Registers/Thread shows the current usage â€” reducing it (via compiler flags or algorithmic changes) allows more warps to fit on each SM."“
^pmsampling:tpc__sm_rf_registers_allocated_shader_cs_realtime.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedRegister OccupancyJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"„
GCompute_Triage.tpc__average_registers_per_thread_shader_cs_realtime.pctAvg Registers/ThreadJgb10x_Compute_Triage_samplingz_Compute_Triage.threads_per_warp = ConversionFactorMetric(32.0, DimUnit.threads / DimUnit.warps)z¢Compute_Triage.tpc__average_registers_per_thread_shader_cs_realtime = RatioMetric(tpc__sm_rf_registers_allocated_shader_cs_realtime, RollupOp.avg, Compute_Triage.threads_per_warp * tpc__warps_active_shader_cs_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 255.0, 'average # of registers per thread, for CS warps')"ÿ
SM Block OccupancyèCheck whether the block-slot limit is the occupancy limiter. If this is near 100% while warp occupancy is low, each block has too few warps â€” increase threads per block, or restructure the work decomposition to merge small blocks."|
Fpmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedAverage CTAs ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"ù
L1TEX Data Occupancy–Shows how much of the on-chip SRAM shared-memory partition is used by resident CTAs vs the total partition size. If allocated is near the partition size and occupancy is low, the per-CTA shared-memory allocation is the binding occupancy limiter â€” check Per-CTA Resource Usage.␀"›
