SysL2 ThroughputÈFind the SysL2 throughput limiter. The SysL2 cache serves system-memory and peer-memory aperture accesses â€” traffic that crosses PCIe, C2C, or NVLink instead of going to local DRAM.
If SysL2 throughput is unexpectedly high, data may be allocated in the wrong memory aperture â€” move hot buffers to device memory (cudaMalloc) and copy data explicitly.
Cross-reference with PCIe/C2C/NVLink bandwidth in the Interconnect group to check for link saturation."Õ
