Top-Level Throughput␀*³
Top-Level ThroughputÐStart here. Compare throughputs and occupancy side-by-side to classify the workload.
If SM Activity and Warp Occupancy are low while all throughputs are low, the GPU is underfilled â€” check Launch & Dispatch for launch sizes and dispatch gaps.
If all throughputs are low but occupancy is moderate, the workload is latency-limited â€” look at SM Occupancy & Stalls for warp scheduling bottlenecks.
If one throughput is clearly dominant (above ~60%), the workload is throughput-limited in that unit â€” drill into the corresponding cache or memory group below.
If both compute and memory throughputs are high (above ~80%), you are near hardware limits â€” validate with DRAM achieved bandwidth and check for tail effects."w
