:TriageCompute.tpc__average_cta_user_latency_realtime.ratioCTA User LatencyJgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingzÝTriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime = CounterMetric(gr__ctas_launched_queue_sync_realtime + gr__ctas_launched_queue_async_realtime, '# of CTAs launched') TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zÒTriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime = CounterMetric(TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime + gr__workids_granted_as_ctas_realtime) TriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zÓTriageCompute.tpc__average_cta_user_latency_realtime = RatioMetric(tpc__ctas_active_realtime, RollupOp.sum, TriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime, RollupOp.sum, 1.0, 'average user CTA duration (cycles)')"‰
"SM Instruction Latency Per Read OpÔAverage cycles a warp stalls waiting for each type of read to complete. Higher values indicate longer memory latency.
High Local/Global Read Latency points to cache misses or poor coalescing â€” check L1TEX Sector Hit Rate and Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Operation.
High Shared Read Latency usually means bank conflicts â€” check Shared Bank Conflict Ratios.
High Texture Read Latency suggests cache thrashing or large working sets â€” check L1TEX Cache Capacity per Warp."Þ
