L1TEX Sector Hit Rate×Cache hit rates per operation type. A low rate means that operation is paying L2/DRAM latency. Atomics always miss in L1 and are not shown.
Low Global LD Hit Rate: improve coalescing (warp-stride patterns) or tile data to fit in L1.
Low Local Hit Rate: spill traffic is thrashing the cache â€” reduce register pressure.
Low Texture Hit Rate: spatial locality is poor or working set is too large â€” consider reducing texture resolution or improving access coherence.
Compare LDGSTS Hit Rate if using asynchronous copy (cp.async) â€” a low rate means the bypassed path is not benefiting from caching."ë
