+pmsampling:pcie__write_bytes.sum.per_secondPCIe Write BandwidthJgb20x_TriageCompute_sampling*‹
InterconnectŠPCIe interconnect utilization. If high, host-device data transfer is a bottleneck â€” check if transfers can be overlapped with compute (using streams), reduced in volume, or eliminated via persistent device-side data.
If PCIe throughput is unexpectedly high during compute-only phases, data may be allocated in system memory and accessed directly over PCIe rather than residing in device DRAM."n
=pmsampling:pcie__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedPCIe ThroughputJgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingŒ
Clock Frequencies␀*ô
Clock FrequenciesãMonitor GPU clock domains over time. Frequency drops during profiling indicate thermal throttling, power capping, or driver clock management.
Compare GPC Frequency (SM/compute clock) with DRAM Frequency â€” if GPC drops while DRAM stays stable, compute throughput is reduced while memory remains constant, shifting the compute-vs-memory balance.
For consistent profiling, lock clocks before measurement. Nsight Compute typically locks the GPC clock, but other domains may still vary."\
