Top-Level Throughput␀*Ñ
Top-Level Throughput¥Start here. Compare throughputs and occupancy side-by-side to classify the workload.
If SM Activity and Warp Occupancy are low while all throughputs are low, the GPU is not filled â€” check Launch & Dispatch for launch sizes and dispatch gaps.
If all throughputs are low but occupancy is moderate, the workload is latency-limited â€” look at SM Occupancy & Stalls for warp scheduling bottlenecks.
If one throughput is clearly dominant (above ~60%), the workload is throughput-limited in that unit â€” drill into the corresponding cache or memory group below.
If both compute and memory throughputs are high (above ~80%), you are near hardware limits â€” check for tail effects."w
Fpmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedBlock OccupancyJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"¾
ATriageCompute.tpc__warps_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedWarp OccupancyJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingi␀␀␀␀␀␀à?zÁTriageCompute.tpc__warps_active = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__warps_active, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.tpc), 'cumulative # of warps in flight') TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active:SetSustainedRate(96.0)"q
;pmsampling:fe__output_ops.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedFront End ThroughputJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"©
>TriageCompute.sm__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedSM ThroughputJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingz¹TriageCompute.sm__throughput = ThroughputMetric({sm__inst_executed_realtime,sm__inst_executed_pipe_aluheavy_realtime,sm__pipe_fma_cycles_active_realtime,sm__pipe_fmaheavy_cycles_active_realtime,sm__inst_executed_pipe_xu_realtime,sm__inst_executed_pipe_uniform_realtime,sm__pipe_tensor_cycles_active_realtime}, '')"Á
ATriageCompute.l1tex__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedL1TEX ThroughputJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzËTriageCompute.l1tex__throughput = ThroughputMetric({l1tex__sram_cycles_array_0_cmd_read,l1tex__sram_cycles_array_0_cmd_write,l1tex__sram_cycles_array_1_cmd_read,l1tex__sram_cycles_array_1_cmd_write,l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts,l1tex__lsu_writeback_active,l1tex__data_pipe_tex_wavefronts,l1tex__f_wavefronts_realtime,l1tex__tex_writeback_active,l1tex__m_xbar2l1tex_read_sectors_realtime,l1tex__samp_wavefronts,tpc__l1tex_m_l1tex2xbar_req_cycles_active}, '')"ñ
?TriageCompute.lts__throughput.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedL2 ThroughputJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingz·TriageCompute.lts__cbc_requests_type_comptag_realtime = CounterMetric(lts__cbc_requests_type_comptag_lookup_hit_realtime + lts__cbc_requests_type_comptag_lookup_miss_or_hit_to_miss_realtime, '# of compressible requests handled by CBC') TriageCompute.lts__cbc_requests_type_comptag_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zÆTriageCompute.lts__throughput = ThroughputMetric({lts__t_sectors_realtime,lts__lts2xbar_cycles_active_realtime,lts__xbar2lts_cycles_active,lts__t_requests,lts__d_atomic_input_cycles_active,TriageCompute.lts__cbc_requests_type_comptag_realtime,lts__d_decomp_input_sectors_realtime,lts__d_sectors_fill_device}, 'LTS Throughput')Þ/
Launch & Dispatch␀"ž
Warps LaunchedœTrack the rate at which new warps are placed onto SMs. Drops or gaps indicate stalls in the dispatch pipeline or periods where no new work is available. Cross-reference with Blocks Launched and engine activity to distinguish supply-side (dispatch) from demand-side (occupancy) limits."m
7pmsampling:tpc__warps_launched_shader_cs.sum.per_secondTotal Warps LaunchedJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"Ó
Warps ActiveÎThe live count of warps occupying SM slots. If Average Warps Active per SM is low (under ~4), the GPU is severely underfilled â€” increase the grid size or block count. If warp count is moderate but SM throughput is still low, the bottleneck is likely warp stalls, not occupancy â€” see SM Occupancy & Stalls for stall classification."¿
5TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage Warps Active per SMJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingi␀␀␀␀␀␀à?zÁTriageCompute.tpc__warps_active = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__warps_active, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.tpc), 'cumulative # of warps in flight') TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active:SetSustainedRate(96.0)"­
5TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Warps ActiveJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÁTriageCompute.tpc__warps_active = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__warps_active, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.tpc), 'cumulative # of warps in flight') TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active:SetSustainedRate(96.0)"°
Blocks LaunchedƒTrack the rate at which thread blocks (CTAs) are launched onto SMs. Drops or pauses reveal dispatch-pipeline stalls. If block launch rate is steady but occupancy is low, the blocks themselves may be resource-heavy â€” check Per-CTA Resource Usage for register or shared-memory pressure.
Compare Total Blocks Launched with Work Distributor CTAs Granted. If granted >> launched, the work distributor is pushing work faster than SMs can accept â€” resource exhaustion (registers, shared memory) is throttling launches."Õ
>TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Blocks LaunchedJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÝTriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime = CounterMetric(gr__ctas_launched_queue_sync_realtime + gr__ctas_launched_queue_async_realtime, '# of CTAs launched') TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)"µ
CTriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Blocks Launched (All)Jgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÝTriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime = CounterMetric(gr__ctas_launched_queue_sync_realtime + gr__ctas_launched_queue_async_realtime, '# of CTAs launched') TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zÒTriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime = CounterMetric(TriageCompute.gr__ctas_launched_realtime + gr__workids_granted_as_ctas_realtime) TriageCompute.gr_total_ctas_launched_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)"„
Epmsampling:gr__workids_granted_as_ctas_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedWork Distributor CTAs GrantedJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"¨
Blocks Launched per QueueœCompare CTA launch rates across sync and async queues. If one queue dominates while the other is idle, consider distributing independent work across both queues for better GPU utilization. Large rate imbalances may also indicate a serialization bottleneck in the host submission path."s
