L2 Sector Hit Rates from L1TEXáL2 hit rates specifically for traffic originating from the SM. Low rates here mean the data is missing both L1 and L2 â€” every such access pays full DRAM or system-memory latency.
Low Read Hit Rate: the working set exceeds L2 capacity, or access patterns are too scattered â€” reduce the active data footprint or improve temporal reuse.
Low Write Hit Rate: many writes are allocating new L2 lines â€” normal for streaming writes but costly for read-modify-write patterns.
Low Atomic Hit Rate: atomic targets are not cached â€” distribute atomic operations across more addresses, or use warp-level reductions."“
