Shared Memory Bandwidth·Effective vs wasted shared-memory bandwidth. Imputed Bandwidth Overhead is bandwidth lost to inactive thread lanes and bank conflicts.
If Overhead is large relative to useful Read/Atom bandwidth, the access pattern is inefficient â€” remap thread-to-bank mapping to reduce conflicts, or ensure warps are fully active.
High Atom bandwidth suggests frequent shared-memory atomics â€” consider warp-level shuffle reductions as an alternative.␀"z
