&L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Hit MissOverall L1 cache effectiveness for tagged memory spaces (local, global). The hit-to-miss ratio directly determines memory latency exposure.
If misses dominate hits, most accesses are paying full L2/DRAM latency â€” focus on improving spatial locality, tiling, or prefetching.
If hits dominate, the L1 cache is working well â€” any remaining throughput issue is likely in the data-stage pipeline, not cache misses.␀"g
