SysL2 Bandwidth per DestinationãSplit SysL2 traffic between system memory (CPU-attached) and peer memory (other GPU).
If SysMem traffic is large, data is crossing PCIe â€” allocate device-memory buffers and use explicit copies.
If PeerMem traffic is large, multi-GPU communication is a factor â€” check whether peer accesses can be batched or replaced with explicit transfers via NVLink.␀"u
