HTriageCompute.syslts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcnode_hub_realtime.pctSysL2 Hit Rate from HUBJgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingz«TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_lookup_miss_realtime, 'of LTS sectors from node HUB that hit') TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)z™TriageCompute.syslts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcnode_hub_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_lookup_hit_realtime, RollupOp.sum, syslts__t_sectors_srcnode_hub_realtime, RollupOp.sum, 1.0, 'proportion of SYSL2 sector lookups from node HUB that hit')"å
%SysL2 Hits per Operation (from L1TEX)ÖPer-operation hit sector counts at SysL2, for traffic originating from the SM. Mirrors the L2 per-operation hits view but for the system-memory aperture.
Compare Read/Write/Atomic hits with total SysL2 sectors in SysL2 Bandwidth per Source Unit to estimate miss rates.
If Atomic Hit is low relative to atomics shown in SysL2 Atomic Sectors per Operation, cross-aperture atomics are not being cached â€” avoid system-memory atomics or aggregate locally before submission.␀"ö
VTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime.sum.per_secondSysL2 Read Hit (from L1TEX)Jgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingzàTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_miss_realtime, '# of SYSLTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all reads that hit') TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)"ý
WTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime.sum.per_secondSysL2 Write Hit (from L1TEX)Jgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingzåTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_miss_realtime, '# of SYSLTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all writes that hit') TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)"ç
VTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime.sum.per_secondSysL2 Atomic Hit (from L1TEX)Jgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingz×TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime)zõTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric((TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime) - (syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_lookup_miss_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_miss_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_miss_realtime), '# of SYSLTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all atomics or reductions that hit') TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)"Ì
/SysL2 Atomic Sectors per Operation (from L1TEX)­Total atomic sector volume arriving at SysL2 from the SM. Compare with SysL2 Atomic Hit in the row above to compute the atomic miss rate. Cross-aperture atomics pay PCIe/NVLink round-trip latency and should be minimized â€” use device-local reductions and only write the final result to system memory."è
KTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime.sum.per_second!SysL2 Atomic Sectors (from L1TEX)Jgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingz×TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime)*Â
SysL2 ThroughputèFind the SysL2 throughput limiter. The SysL2 cache serves system-memory and peer-memory aperture accesses â€” traffic that crosses PCIe or NVLink instead of going to local DRAM.
If SysL2 throughput is unexpectedly high, data may be allocated in the wrong memory aperture â€” move hot buffers to device memory (cudaMalloc) and copy data explicitly.
If both SysL2 and L2 (SysMem Path) show traffic, cross-reference with PCIe Bandwidth in the Interconnect group to check for PCIe saturation."v
