SM Compute Pipelines␀"™
Executed IPC¢Compare IPC against active cycles vs elapsed cycles. A large gap between Active and Elapsed IPC means the SM spends significant time idle â€” check occupancy and dispatch cadence.
If Active IPC itself is low (well under 1.0), warps are stalling frequently â€” see Warp Stall Reasons for the dominant stall class.
If Active IPC is healthy but Elapsed IPC is low, the problem is GPU utilization, not per-warp efficiency."o
:pmsampling:sm__inst_executed_realtime.avg.per_cycle_activeExecuted IPC ActiveJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"q
;pmsampling:sm__inst_executed_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedExecuted IPC ElapsedJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"ç
Active Threads Per WarpöThe total height shows the fraction of active thread lanes per warp instruction. Lower than 100% means branch divergence or partial-warp launches are wasting SIMT lanes.
If Pred Off is large, many threads are executing but predicated-off â€” the math pipe does work that is discarded. Restructure branches to reduce divergence, or consider warp-level masking strategies.
If overall thread utilization is low, check whether launch block sizes are warp-aligned (multiples of 32).
Per-pipe pred-on counters (FMA, FMA Heavy) break down which math pipes carry the divergence burden â€” see Per-Pipe Thread-Instruction Throughput below."Ú
UTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime.pctPred On per ExecutedJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÌTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime = RatioMetric(sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on_realtime, RollupOp.avg, sm__inst_executed_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 32.0, '')"ó
VTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_off_per_inst_executed_realtime.pctPred Off per ExecutedJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingz„TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_off_realtime = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__thread_inst_executed, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.sm) - sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on_realtime) TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_off_realtime:SetSustainedRate(128.0)zÜTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_off_per_inst_executed_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_off_realtime, RollupOp.avg, sm__inst_executed_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 32.0, '')"Ù
&Per-Pipe Thread-Instruction Throughput†Absolute thread-instruction rates per pipe, split by predication. Compare FMA and FMA Heavy pred-on rates to see which pipe carries the most useful work. If Pred Off (All) is large relative to the pred-on totals, a significant fraction of SIMT lanes execute with their results discarded â€” restructure divergent branches to reduce wasted work.
Cross-reference with Active Threads Per Warp: if pred-off percentage is high above AND one pipes pred-on throughput is low here, that pipes code paths are heavily divergent."¼
OTriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fma_pred_on_realtime.sum.per_secondFMA Thread-Inst Pred OnJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingz±TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fma_pred_on_realtime = CounterMetric(sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fmaheavy_type_fp32_pred_on_realtime + sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fmaheavy_type_int_pred_on_realtime + sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fma_type_fp16_pred_on_realtime + sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fmalite_type_fp32_pred_on_realtime) TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pipe_fma_pred_on_realtime:SetSustainedRate(128.0)"×
